# Beginner Piano

> A playable piano in the browser — press keyboard keys to play notes, built with vanilla HTML, CSS, and JavaScript.

---

## Overview

A lightweight browser-based piano covering 17 keys across two octaves (C to E). White and black keys are mapped to keyboard shortcuts and light up on press. Audio is played via HTML `<audio>` elements triggered by `keydown` events. No frameworks, no dependencies.

---

## Key Mapping

| Key | Note | | Key | Note |
|-----|------|-|-----|------|
| `A` | C    | | `H` | A    |
| `W` | C#   | | `U` | A#   |
| `S` | D    | | `J` | B    |
| `E` | D#   | | `K` | C    |
| `D` | E    | | `O` | C#   |
| `F` | F    | | `L` | D    |
| `T` | F#   | | `P` | D#   |
| `G` | G    | | `;` | E    |
| `Y` | G#   | | | |

---

## Features

- 17 playable keys — 10 white, 7 black (sharps)
- Keyboard shortcut hints displayed on each key
- Visual key press animation on click and keydown
- Audio playback via external WAV files
- Zero dependencies — pure vanilla JS

---

## Getting Started

No build step. Just open in a browser:

```bash
git clone https://github.com/illusionoftalha/beginnner_piano.git
cd beginnner_piano
# open index.html in your browser
```

> **Note:** Audio is streamed from an external host. An internet connection is required for sound to work.

---

## Project Structure

```
beginnner_piano/
├── index.html   # Piano markup and audio elements
├── style.css    # Key styling, black/white layout, press animation
└── main.js      # keydown listener and audio playback logic
```

